Logo, a turtle graphics language, written in BBC BASIC for DreamRISC.

Type commands in the box under the canvas and press Return, or pick one
from Demos on the menu. Run, Stop and Clear do what they say. Up and down
step through what you typed.

  REPEAT 4 [FD 100 RT 90]

  TO SQUARE :SIZE
    REPEAT 4 [FD :SIZE RT 90]
  END

Coordinates are 200 steps left and right of centre, 140 up and down.
Colours for SETPC are the usual Logo 0 to 15, mapped to the nearest desktop
colour; there is no magenta.

Procedures can be written in Edit and dropped on the window to load them.
LOAD "file and SAVE "file work on a floppy, e.g. SAVE "ADFS::0.$.Mine
